A||N||2||MikeSchaefer||Where to get the best Steering Rack?||||5||
Z||000000||MikeSchaefer||09-24-2000||01:13 PM||||Hi,  I'm looking at replacement Steering Racks right now for my 84 V-6.  I saw that the fiero store sells one for $200 reconditioned.  Is this the best one available?  Or do any other places sell the racks?  What should I look at when buying one?  Will a later model rack fit my 84?  I would really like an 85 or 87 one.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-24-2000||02:24 PM||||There are only 2 diferant rack units for all 84-87 fiero I know of.<P>the diferance is in number of turns lock to lock. the base coupes are mostly 3.5 turns the SC SE and GT ones are 3 turns. Otherwise they are all the same to the best of my knowledge.<P>There may be other racks that fit Fiero. The issue there is most likely the length of the inner tie rods. <P>The other question is do they accept the steering stabilizer and if not is that an issue to you. Some people here have removed it and are perfectly happy it's gone.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MikeSchaefer||09-24-2000||03:44 PM||||Hi,<BR>Thanks for the response.  Would the 3 turn rack fit in my 84 base coupe?  <BR>Thanks again,<BR>Michael Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||5
